706 0 obj
<<
/Title (The system maintains the current number of occupied seats, the number of waiting groups, and an estimated waiting time. It also provides a simple customer-decision calculation using travel time and estimated restaurant waiting time.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 333 0 R
/Prev 486 0 R
/Next 707 0 R
>>
endobj
707 0 obj
<<
/Title (The current implementation is intentionally console-based and uses beginner-level Python concepts. The input buttons or camera layer are not implemented in this version; occupancy and queue values are entered through the program menu. This keeps the project aligned with the Python for Beginners course while leaving a clear path for future sensor or computer-vision integration.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 333 0 R
/Prev 706 0 R
/Next 487 0 R
>>
endobj
708 0 obj
<<
/Title (Restaurant customers often make decisions using only distance or opening status. A restaurant that is close may still require a long wait, while a farther restaurant may have seats available immediately. There is therefore a need for a simple system that combines restaurant occupancy, waiting queue information, and estimated waiting time into one usable view.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 488 0 R
/Next 754 0 R
>>
endobj
709 0 obj
<<
/Title (Proposed solution: Build a modular Python application that accepts occupancy and queue inputs, validates them, stores the current state, estimates waiting time, and calculates total customer time by combining travel time with expected waiting time.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 488 0 R
/Prev 754 0 R
>>
endobj
